Notebook[{
Cell["Tensor Decomposition for e+e- \[LongRightArrow] \[Pi]+\[Pi]- at One \
Loop", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d51470bb-7ff4-4ab1-abbd-193f1624b583"],

Cell["\<\
Same process and same basis as the tree-level notebook (ee_pipi_FF_Tree.nb), \
now for the bare one-loop amplitude in scalar QED. The form factors F1, F2 \
are obtained in two independent ways: (A) project the amplitude on the basis \
with D-dimensional spin sums and reduce the resulting scalar loop integrals \
with TID, solving G.F = B as at tree level; (B) tensor-reduce the open \
amplitude first and read the two coefficients off directly with the Dirac \
equation, so no Gram matrix has to be inverted. Both are then reduced to \
scalar Passarino-Veltman functions A0, B0, C0, D0 and compared.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"966e3f36-d70e-4027-8901-c7648cf00230"],

Cell["1. Packages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"871605e1-9cb3-4166-801e-9802faf2e66e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$FeynCalcStartupMessages", " ", "=", " ", "False"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$LoadAddOns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\"\<FeynArts\>\"", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", "\"\<FeynCalc`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionU\
UID->"aba9b84e-2c12-4571-a635-30791fba63fc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$FAVerbose", " ", "=", " ", "0"}], ";"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"0c97872a-6a5f-4aed-a6c7-aa092fe2ce31"],

Cell["2. Kinematics", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"527b43a2-114e-4985-8b8e-6f302006e254"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FCClearScalarProducts", "[", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"me", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SMP", "[", "\"\<m_e\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mpi", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SMP", "[", "\"\<m_pi\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SetMandelstam", "[", 
   RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "t", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"me", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mpi", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "s", " ", "-", " ", "t"}], ",",
     " ", "p1", ",", " ", "p2", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"-", "p3"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"-", "p4"}], ",", " ", "me", ",", " ", "me", ",", " ", "mpi", ",",
     " ", "mpi"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"s", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"me", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"mpi", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"626bac12-f54b-4fef-89ca-5f172b02a972"],

Cell["3. One-loop diagrams", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6eba79ea-49fd-4ee1-8855-b3aa45ff522e"],

Cell["\<\
Scalar QED is again obtained from the FeynArts SM model by keeping only the \
photon, the electron and the charged Goldstone boson S[3]. Compared to tree \
level three more things have to be removed: the muon and tau (they would run \
in the vacuum-polarisation loop), the quartic S[3] self-coupling (a \
Higgs-sector artefact, not part of sQED; its single diagram vanishes anyway \
by current conservation) and, via ExcludeTopologies, tadpoles and \
external-leg corrections. The latter means this is the bare, unrenormalised \
1PI amplitude: UV poles do not cancel and would be removed by on-shell \
counterterms.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11100152-2c2e-4310-b95a-042c98e915cf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tops", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CreateTopologies", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ExcludeTopologies", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Tadpoles", ",", " ", "WFCorrections"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"diags", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"InsertFields", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tops", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"F", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"F", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Model", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SM\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InsertionLevel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "Particles", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ExcludeParticles", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"F", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"F", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"F", "[", "4", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"F", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"F", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "3", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"V", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"V", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"S", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"S", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"U", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"U", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"U", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"U", "[", "4", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ExcludeFieldPoints", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FieldPoint", "[", "_", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"S", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Paint", "[", 
   RowBox[{"diags", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ColumnsXRows", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Numbering", " ", "->", " ", "Simple"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"SheetHeader", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"900", ",", " ", "360"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",Exp\
ressionUUID->"e917f826-0b9b-4344-8250-befeced7a9f4"],

Cell["4. Amplitudes", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2b2bfdc4-e71c-4353-84c6-458a6da0966a"],

Cell["\<\
The amplitudes are kept as a list, one per diagram, in D dimensions with loop \
momentum q. Each diagram is labelled by the masses of the propagators that \
carry q, which identifies its class unambiguously.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"465b5143-b1a4-4daf-82b6-cfc2a59e72c8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ampList", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FCFAConvert", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"CreateFeynAmp", "[", "diags", "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"IncomingMomenta", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p1", ",", " ", "p2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"OutgoingMomenta", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p3", ",", " ", "p4"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LoopMomenta", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "q", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"UndoChiralSplittings", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ChangeDimension", " ", "->", " ", "D"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"List", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"SMP", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Contract", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"DropSumOver", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FinalSubstitutions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"SMP", "[", "\"\<m_W\>\"", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "mpi"}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nDiag", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "ampList", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"loopMasses", "[", "a_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sort", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"PropagatorDenominator", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Momentum", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "___"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "m_"}], "]"}], 
        " ", "/;", " ", 
        RowBox[{"!", " ", 
         RowBox[{"FreeQ", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "q"}], "]"}]}]}], " ", ":>", " ", "m"}], ",",
       " ", "Infinity"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"className", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "me"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<two-photon exchange, seagull triangle\>\""}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "me", ",", " ", "me"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<electron vertex correction\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "mpi", ",", " ", "mpi"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<pion vertex correction\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "me", ",", " ", "mpi"}], "}"}], 
      " ", "->", " ", "\"\<two-photon exchange, box\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "mpi"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<pion vertex, seagull bubble\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "mpi", "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<photon self-energy, seagull tadpole\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"me", ",", " ", "me"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<vacuum polarisation, electron loop\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"mpi", ",", " ", "mpi"}], "}"}], " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<vacuum polarisation, pion loop\>\""}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"labels", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
      RowBox[{"className", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Key", "[", 
        RowBox[{"loopMasses", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<?\>\""}],
       "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "ampList"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nDiag", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"loopMasses", " ", "/@", " ", "ampList"}], ",", " ", "labels"}],
      "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<diagram\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<loop propagator masses\>\"", 
        ",", " ", "\"\<class\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",Expr\
essionUUID->"3f200442-5367-40fd-a845-3a332362619d"],

Cell["5. Basis and Gram matrix in D dimensions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2750b9f3-3213-4239-b90d-948d584fa612"],

Cell["\<\
The same two structures as at tree level, built from D-dimensional spinors \
and gamma matrices (SpinorVBarD, SpinorUD, GSD) since the amplitude is in D \
dimensions. The Gram matrix carries no explicit D because no index \
contraction occurs in it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50accdac-14e5-4716-9a2e-28f0cf1d9ae4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"vbar", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SpinorVBarD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p1", ",", " ", "me"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"uSp", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SpinorUD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p2", ",", " ", "me"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"T1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"vbar", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"GSD", "[", "p3", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "uSp"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"T2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"vbar", " ", ".", " ", "uSp"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"basis", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"T1", ",", " ", "T2"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"spinSum", "[", "expr_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FermionSpinSum", "[", "expr", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"G", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Factor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"spinSum", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"basis", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"ComplexConjugate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"basis", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "basis", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "basis", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"G", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"b09dd121-837c-4fa2-9d72-e9ad8bfa0b7b"],

Cell["6. Route A: project, then reduce the loop integrals", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e79bc4c0-2deb-4e47-bc4d-1dca711d1c7b"],

Cell["\<\
B_i = \[Sum]_spins T_i^* M is a Dirac trace containing the loop momentum. TID \
performs the Passarino-Veltman tensor reduction; UsePaVeBasis keeps the \
tensor coefficient functions (C1, C12, D001, ...) instead of reducing \
everything to scalar integrals at once, which keeps the expressions small and \
avoids inverse Gram determinants at this stage. The remaining tree-level \
photon propagator 1/(p1+p2)^2 is made explicit afterwards.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"735567b1-559d-4f44-8d5c-0c2f4a73c462"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"loopReduce", "[", "expr_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", 
    RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
     RowBox[{"expr", ",", " ", "q", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"UsePaVeBasis", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ToPaVe", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"formFactorsA", "[", "amp_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "B", "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"B", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"loopReduce", "[", 
          RowBox[{"spinSum", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"ComplexConjugate", "[", 
             RowBox[{"basis", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "amp"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Length", "[", "basis", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"LinearSolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{"G", ",", " ", "B"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FA", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"formFactorsA", " ", "/@", " ", "ampList"}]}], ";"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e5f4f5ed-e393-\
443e-98f8-947101c4a2e1"],

Cell["\<\
Each diagram is then reduced to scalar integrals with PaVeReduce and written \
with the conventional heads A0, B0, C0, D0. This step is cheap here and makes \
cancellations visible that are hidden in the tensor-coefficient basis: F2 of \
the pion vertex correction, for instance, is a combination of C1, B0 and C0 \
that is identically zero.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"91cbf074-dbea-44c8-901c-1d079c551c94"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FAred", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"PaVeToABCD", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
          RowBox[{"PaVeReduce", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "FA", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"98b8b127-3119-\
4617-b508-1ab6bfe55c4c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nDiag", "]"}], ",", " ", "labels", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"LeafCount", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"LeafCount", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<diagram\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<class\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<size F1\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<size F2\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cb874ab8-3ac3-4ef7-afbe-\
3f419bcc13ea"],

Cell["\<\
F2 vanishes for every diagram that only corrects the photon propagator or the \
\[Pi]\[Pi]\[Gamma] vertex: such a correction multiplies the conserved \
electron current by a vertex function whose (p3+p4) part drops out, so it \
only rescales the tree structure. Only diagrams with a loop attached to the \
electron line (electron vertex, seagull triangle, boxes) feed the \
helicity-flip structure vbar u.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"477e2e05-985b-47fe-913c-acf6e8da706a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"vpPos", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
     RowBox[{"labels", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"_String", "?", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"StringContainsQ", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<vacuum\>\"", " ", "|", " ", "\"\<tadpole\>\""}]}], 
          "]"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"labels", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "vpPos", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"vpPos", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"11892fe0-a6c1-49df-90dc-982ff8dfae0b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"evPos", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
      RowBox[{"labels", ",", " ", "\"\<electron vertex correction\>\""}], 
      "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"evPos", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"3f45fb64-7aeb-419c-abb3-aaa73956d27b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"evPos", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"844dc411-d9a5-4486-bd5d-c7cacc370457"],

Cell["\<\
7. Route B: reduce the open amplitude, then use the Dirac equation\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d1e780d0-abfc-4ac8-b866-6d0c4177f3e7"],

Cell["\<\
Here TID acts on the amplitude with the spinor chain still open. After \
eliminating p4 by momentum conservation, DiracSimplify applies the Dirac \
equation (vbar(p1) p1slash = -m_e vbar(p1), p2slash u(p2) = m_e u(p2)) and \
only the two basis structures survive, so F1 and F2 can be read off as \
coefficients. No Gram matrix is needed. The seagull triangle is a good \
illustration: before the Dirac equation its vector structure is vbar (2 \
p2slash - p3slash - p4slash) u, which collapses entirely onto m_e vbar u.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5839af0b-27cb-4eba-a2a6-a3e53c06b497"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"structuresOf", "[", "expr_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Union", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"FCDiracIsolate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"expr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Head", " ", "->", " ", "ds"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ds", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":>", " ", "x"}], ",", " ", 
      "Infinity"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sgPos", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "labels", ",", " ", "\"\<two-photon exchange, seagull triangle\>\""}], 
      "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"seagull", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"loopReduce", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ampList", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "sgPos", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"structuresOf", "[", "seagull", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"f0f7fa08-a221-4dfa-b76d-6d12c08892b2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"structuresOf", "[", 
  RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FCReplaceMomenta", "[", 
    RowBox[{"seagull", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p4", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"p1", " ", "+", " ", "p2", " ", "-", " ", "p3"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8935fb56-09eb-4385-8051-\
5e530f88a558"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"formFactorsB", "[", "amp_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "iso"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{"FCReplaceMomenta", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"loopReduce", "[", "amp", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"p4", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"p1", " ", "+", " ", "p2", " ", "-", " ", "p3"}]}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"iso", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FCDiracIsolate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Head", " ", "->", " ", "ds"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ds", "[", "y_", "]"}], " ", ":>", " ", 
         RowBox[{"If", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"FreeQ", "[", 
            RowBox[{"y", ",", " ", "DiracGamma"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ff2", ",",
            " ", "ff1"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
          RowBox[{"iso", ",", " ", "ff1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
          RowBox[{"iso", ",", " ", "ff2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FB", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"formFactorsB", " ", "/@", " ", "ampList"}]}], ";"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7ba38c26-7ad5-\
4efe-84b9-28f76e4164e5"],

Cell["\<\
Route B is about three times faster since no traces are taken. The two \
results are not identical symbol by symbol: TID produces tensor coefficient \
functions whose arguments are ordered differently in the two routes, and \
relations among them (e.g. C1 in terms of B0 and C0) are not visible to \
Simplify. After PaVeReduce, which rewrites everything in terms of scalar \
functions, the difference vanishes diagram by diagram.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a12d118-89f2-4b32-8cb0-4ba77c67dd49"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"PaVeReduce", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FA", " ", "-", " ", "FB"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "nDiag"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"156e1a8f-6ca1-4859-866d-5a0ef8e2ab5c"],

Cell["8. The one-loop form factors", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"66b9ecbc-3635-48fd-a91e-b0558b3f4c3e"],

Cell["\<\
Total bare one-loop form factors, fully reduced to scalar integrals and \
written with the conventional heads A0, B0, C0, D0. Fifteen scalar integrals \
appear: two tadpoles, five bubbles, six triangles and the two boxes. The C0 \
and D0 functions with two massless photon propagators are IR divergent; in \
dimensional regularisation their soft poles sit inside the PaVe symbols and \
cancel against real emission.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"851b4ff3-a251-4f41-88b2-cb070b740b98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"F1L", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "FAred", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",ExpressionU\
UID->"0777ac56-1a1b-4934-a57b-0426b46c5da4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scalarIntegrals", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Union", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
     RowBox[{"F1L", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
        "A0", " ", "|", " ", "B0", " ", "|", " ", "C0", " ", "|", " ", "D0"}],
         ")"}], "[", "__", "]"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "scalarIntegrals", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", "scalarIntegrals", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"036870cb-7937-4446-9140-17d54cff922b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"LeafCount", " ", "/@", " ", "F1L"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a36134f5-65b1-47db-bd05-f9c82865b2b0"],

Cell["\<\
F1, organised by scalar integral. The denominators show the two sources of \
spurious singularities of the Passarino-Veltman reduction: the Gram \
determinant of the basis (same polynomial as at tree level) and the kinematic \
factors s - 4m_e^2, s - 4m_\[Pi]^2 from the reduction of the tensor bubbles \
and triangles.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26aff812-84cd-4d3a-b184-d31a625cd7d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Collect2", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"F1L", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"A0", ",", " ", "B0", ",", " ", "C0", ",", " ", "D0"}], "}"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Factoring", " ", "->", " ", "Factor"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",Expressi\
onUUID->"a0383b4b-a364-4b41-afbb-6167ceb67a37"],

Cell["\<\
F2 is a helicity-flip amplitude: every term carries a factor m_e (the \
A0(m_e^2) term because A0(m^2) is itself proportional to m^2), so F2 vanishes \
for m_e -> 0 up to the mass logarithms inside the IR-sensitive C0 and D0. It \
is UV finite, as it must be: no counterterm has the structure vbar u.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cafb7583-2809-4bf9-b82d-4687a1ce8ce7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Collect2", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"F1L", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"A0", ",", " ", "B0", ",", " ", "C0", ",", " ", "D0"}], "}"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Factoring", " ", "->", " ", "Factor"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",Expressi\
onUUID->"e4fc523e-6d19-4d39-b16b-9c7b9fb45f90"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"uvPole", "[", "expr_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"PaVeUVPart", "[", "expr", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"D", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "eps"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"eps", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"uvPole", " ", "/@", " ", "F1L"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"a36a5d12-121a-40be-9810-7a2ecd7b99a8"],

Cell["\<\
Relative to the tree-level F1 = -2e^2/s this is a UV pole of -e^2/(6 \[Pi]^2 \
eps), i.e. -(2\[Alpha]/3\[Pi])/eps with FeynCalc's normalisation of the loop \
measure. It is the pole of the unrenormalised 1PI amplitude: charge \
renormalisation removes the vacuum-polarisation part and the vertex \
counterterms, together with the external-leg corrections excluded above, \
remove the rest. Per diagram class:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9197e8f-62c4-48d6-b750-39736f4a7baf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"labels", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"uvPole", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"uvPole", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FAred", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<class\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<UV pole F1\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<UV pole F2\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",Expre\
ssionUUID->"7b8f6eba-bc95-4105-ab4d-f7d184d201ec"],

Cell["9. Save", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"90159f92-f8f8-4566-887e-aad8dc06e516"],

Cell["\<\
The fully reduced one-loop form factors (scalar A0, B0, C0, D0 basis, \
D-dimensional) are written into the folder ee_pipi next to the notebook, \
alongside the tree-level results.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8d2ae5d-4129-4cfd-b49f-c82f57259757"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"outDir", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Quiet", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Check", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directory", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "\"\<ee_pipi\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"If", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"!", " ", 
     RowBox[{"DirectoryQ", "[", "outDir", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"CreateDirectory", "[", "outDir", "]"}]}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Do", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Put", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"F1L", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"outDir", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<FF_1L_\>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "i", "]"}], " ", "<>", 
          " ", "\"\<.m\>\""}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Length", "[", "basis", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FileNames", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<*\>\"", ",", " ", "outDir"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"f34e9f02-8793-47e3-baa6-ef83de70069a"],

Cell["10. Other ways to do this", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0057f26a-7a39-40f7-8d1a-ab0119b3739d"],

Cell["\<\
Passarino-Veltman (used here). TID with UsePaVeBasis followed by PaVeReduce \
is the classic route and fully automatic. Its price is the inverse Gram \
determinants: the coefficients of the scalar integrals have spurious poles at \
the thresholds and at the boundary of phase space, which cause numerical \
cancellations. For numerics one would evaluate the A0...D0 with LoopTools or \
Collier (FeynHelpers provides LToolsEvaluate), or expand them analytically in \
eps with Package-X (LoopRefine).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bcd30b78-9d92-48a1-9be5-03072e6dbc49"],

Cell["\<\
Projectors plus IBP reduction. Route A computes the projections B_i = \
\[Sum]_spins T_i^* M as scalar Feynman integrals with numerators q.p_j. \
Instead of PV, one can map these onto integral families \
(FCLoopFindTopologies, FCLoopTensorReduce, FCLoopToPakForm in FeynCalc 10) \
and reduce them to master integrals with LiteRed, Kira or FIRE. The number of \
masters is small (here the same fifteen as above, but chosen so that no Gram \
determinants appear in the coefficients), the method extends directly to two \
loops, and the masters can be evaluated with differential equations or \
numerically (pySecDec, AMFlow).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0230d282-9d8a-4284-8505-fe0d07abf32a"],

Cell["\<\
Helicity amplitudes. Instead of form factors one can evaluate the helicity \
amplitudes directly in the spinor-helicity formalism (S@M, SpinorsExtras), as \
done in the \[Pi]\[Pi]\[Gamma] notebook. For a 2 -> 2 process with two \
structures the form-factor language is simpler, but for ee -> \[Pi]\[Pi]\
\[Gamma] (eight structures) helicity amplitudes avoid an 8 x 8 Gram matrix.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79e076a8-bd6a-476a-8aff-bdcdee46b46d"],

Cell["\<\
Scheme remarks. The basis here is D-dimensional (CDR). In the 't \
Hooft-Veltman or FDH schemes the external structures are kept \
four-dimensional and only the loop is continued; the projectors are then \
D-dimensional only in the traces, and F1, F2 differ by finite rational terms \
that cancel in physical quantities. For a massive QED process without \
\[Gamma]5 there is no scheme ambiguity in the Dirac algebra itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d094abe-a618-4db3-b343-3bf335438228"]
},
WindowSize->{1200, 850},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
